  "doubts": "The circuit starts and ends at Halfmoon Bay, walking roads to Horseshoe Bay and Lee Bay first; no road end feature is clearly in Halfmoon Bay, so the start/end ref is the Halfmoon Bay coast name T20 (the settlement lies in the bay). Lee Bay, the park entrance where the track begins, is given as F2 (North West Circuit Track meets Lee Bay Road). F1 (unnamed track meets Main Road) may be where the former Kaipipi Road reaches the settlement, but the text does not say, so it is not used. No direction is stated; the page describes the circuit from Halfmoon Bay via Port William first. The text says the track passes inland from Gull Rock Point and reaches a lookout over East Ruggedy Beach before descending to a river crossing; whether the beach itself is walked is not clear. Big Hellfire Hut is also called 'Hellfire Pass Hut' in the text. Duck Creek T14 is the one near Mason Bay. The Features section mentions flying in to Mason Bay and walking to the Freshwater River as an option for those not doing the multi-day tramp; it is not recorded as a way of this circuit."
